                      "id": "lOHjg",
                      "name": "aiP1",
                      "fill": "$--foreground",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Building accessible React components requires attention to semantic HTML, ARIA attributes, and keyboard navigation. Here are the key practices:",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": "$--font-size-sm",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "U034a",
                      "name": "aiP2",
                      "fill": "$--foreground",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "1. Use semantic elements like <button>, <nav>, <main> instead of generic <div> elements [1]. This provides built-in accessibility without extra ARIA roles.\n\n2. Manage focus properly — trap focus in modals, restore focus on close, and ensure logical tab order [2][3].\n\n3. Support keyboard interactions for all interactive elements. Custom components should respond to Enter, Space, Escape, and arrow keys as users expect [4].",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": "$--font-size-sm",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
